1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:01,580
Loopback Transformer:

2
00:00:01,580 --> 00:00:04,890
towards a unified view of
residual looped Transformers.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:10,770
Looped Transformers apply the
same blocks again and again.

4
00:00:11,560 --> 00:00:12,750
Sharing fixes the weights,

5
00:00:12,960 --> 00:00:15,270
but not how each update is reused.

6
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:20,170
Addition gives every update weight one,

7
00:00:20,380 --> 00:00:22,450
so the total grows with depth.

8
00:00:23,240 --> 00:00:25,680
A joint softmax shares one unit of weight,

9
00:00:25,680 --> 00:00:27,210
so the input shrinks.

10
00:00:27,980 --> 00:00:30,210
Loopback keeps the input at one;

11
00:00:30,620 --> 00:00:31,730
decay sets the total,

12
00:00:32,080 --> 00:00:33,710
and attention allocates it.

13
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:36,790
The recipe:

14
00:00:37,120 --> 00:00:38,030
store updates,

15
00:00:38,440 --> 00:00:39,270
not outputs;

16
00:00:39,660 --> 00:00:41,630
keep the input on its own path;

17
00:00:42,120 --> 00:00:43,590
let decay set the total,

18
00:00:43,940 --> 00:00:45,390
and attention allocate it.

19
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:49,810
From 191M to 3B parameters,

20
00:00:50,480 --> 00:00:54,170
Loopback reaches lower validation
loss than the standard Transformer,

21
00:00:54,340 --> 00:00:57,330
with 40–75% of its parameters.

22
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:00,970
At 374M,

23
00:01:01,340 --> 00:01:06,250
it is the best of nine models in
both loss and thirteen-task average.

24
00:01:07,500 --> 00:01:10,590
Run more loops at
inference than in training,

25
00:01:10,960 --> 00:01:13,970
and Loopback degrades far
less than plain addition.

26
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:20,590
The read adds under 0.1% in FLOPs;

27
00:01:20,860 --> 00:01:21,930
at 3B,

28
00:01:22,620 --> 00:01:26,570
training runs within 6% of the
standard Transformer's speed.

29
00:01:28,400 --> 00:01:29,590
Store updates.

30
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:32,130
Keep the input on its own path.

31
00:01:32,640 --> 00:01:33,630
Decay sets the total;

32
00:01:34,100 --> 00:01:34,950
attention allocates it.

